@startuml TimelineEditorDomainModel
title Dionysus Timeline Editor - Canonical Domain Model
hide methods
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class Project {
  id
  schemaVersion
  rootCompositionId
  assets[]
  shots[]
}
class CompositionDocument {
  id
  kind
  canvasSettings
  tracks[]
  placements[]
}
class Track {
  id
  kind
  order
  muted
}
class CompositionPlacement {
  id
  trackId
  start
  duration
  sourceIn
  sourceOut
  sourceRef
  transform
}
class SourceRef {
  kind
  assetId
  versionId
  compositionId
}
class ClipAsset {
  id
  versions[]
}
class ClipVersion {
  id
  compositionDocument
}
class Shot {
  id
  versions[]
}
class ShotVersion {
  id
  mediaAssetId
  provenance
}
class EditCommand {
  type
  targetIds[]
  payload
  validate()
  apply()
  invert()
}

Project "1" *-- "1" CompositionDocument : root composition
Project "1" o-- "*" ClipAsset : owns
Project "1" o-- "*" Shot : owns
ClipAsset "1" *-- "*" ClipVersion : versions
Shot "1" *-- "*" ShotVersion : alternatives
CompositionDocument "1" *-- "*" Track
CompositionDocument "1" *-- "*" CompositionPlacement
CompositionPlacement "*" --> "1" Track
CompositionPlacement "*" --> "1" SourceRef : pinned source
EditCommand ..> CompositionDocument : validated transaction

note bottom of CompositionPlacement
A versioned placement pins a concrete source/version.
Creating a new Shot Version does not silently repoint it.
end note
note bottom of ClipVersion
compositionDocument is canonical.
Legacy arrays are read-compatible projections during migration,
not a second writable source of truth.
end note
@enduml
